<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50187" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vāra</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A wooden horse</i> or <i>trestle</i>
			for spreading nets upon; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence, prov.: sequitur varam vibia,</span>”
				<i>one evil follows the other</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 12 praef.</span></i>
			 monos.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A forked pole</i> for spreading nets upon, <i><span class="en">Luc. 4,
			439</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">to support a bough,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					5, 9, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>